you know, a local quarterback getting $500 to do a radio ad for a car dealership.

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:49.680
The entire financial paradigm of college sports has inverted.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:55.000
It has transformed into a massive unregulated shadow economy.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:00.920
Wealthy university alumni are pooling their money together to form what are called collectives.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:06.000
These collectives operate as independent limited liability companies, totally separate from

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.680
the university's official athletic budget.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:13.640
They are essentially operating as unregulated payroll departments, distributing highly lucrative

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:17.040
endorsement contracts to keep top talent on the roster.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:20.360
It used to be that you only stayed in college for five or six years if you weren't quite

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:21.880
good enough to get drafted.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:25.640
You stayed because the NFL or the NBA wasn't calling.

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:31.000
But today, because of these collectives, college sports is the professional league for many

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.000
of these players.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.000
Exactly.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.880
We are talking about athletes making high six figures, sometimes even seven figures, while

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.880
they are supposedly amateur students.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:44.000
If your peak earning window is happening right now at age 22 and you know you are likely

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:49.560
going to be a career backup in the NFL making the league minimum or perhaps not make a professional

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:54.480
roster at all, your financial incentive is to stretch your college eligibility out as long

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:55.840
as humanly possible.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.360
The collegiate minor leagues are often paying significantly better than the actual lower

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.640
tier pro leagues.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:06.800
And now the NCAA is stepping in and aggressively trying to slam that lucrative earning

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:09.960
window shut after exactly five years.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:15.760
It's like the NCAA is trying to enforce a strict 55 mile per hour speed limit on a highway after

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:20.040
they've already let everyone drive unregulated Formula One cars for the last three years.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:25.640
It is a profound clash between an institution stubbornly clinging to the traditional outdated

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:31.120
concept of amateurism and a labor force that is operating in a completely unbridled free

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:32.800
market economy.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:38.000
When we pull all of these threads together, the overarching narrative is incredibly clear.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:43.040
We are watching massive foundational institutions completely buckle under the weight of rapidly

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.440
accelerating realities.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:47.040
The core issue is institutional lag.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:51.160
The reality on the ground whether it's driven by cutting edge technology, contested scientific

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:55.600
research or modern sports economics is moving at absolute light speed.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:59.960
Meanwhile, the legal and regulatory systems designed to manage that reality are still moving

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.800
at a bureaucratic crawl.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:06.360
And the most important question is who is caught in the crossfire of all these massive

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:08.360
tectonic shifts?

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:09.680
You are.

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:13.480
Regular people are the ones absorbing the shock while the rules of everyday life are

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.080
being rewritten from the top down.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:20.560
It is you standing in the aisle at the hardware store holding a bottle of weed killer having

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:26.200
to blindly guess what the actual cancer risk is because the legal system just gave the manufacturer

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.800
a pass on warning labels to avoid administrative headaches.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:35.120
It is you deciding to just tough it out with a dying five year old laptop because artificial

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:40.640
intelligence supply chain constraints have made a basic replacement completely unaffordable.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:45.920
It is the 20 year old athlete having to hire a federal lawyer just to fight for their right

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:50.280
to maximize their personal earning potential in a system that generates billions of dollars

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:51.560
off their labor.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:56.280
Technological, scientific and financial advancements are moving exponentially faster than the systems

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.480
designed to protect and regulate us.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:02.640
And at the end of the day, individual consumers are the ones left holding the bill.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:05.640
That is the definitive takeaway from the stack of sources.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:10.520
The friction between rapid innovation and sluggish regulation is only going to accelerate.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:14.640
To see how this plays out in real time, there are two specific things you should watch for

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:15.640
next.

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:19.440
First, keep an eye on the Apple iPhone 18 launch scheduled for this fall.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:25.320
Supply chain analysts are already bracing for a retail price hike of up to $200.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:30.560
If you see that jump, eye inflation is officially an entrenched economic reality and regarding

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:34.480
the NCAA pay very close attention this Wednesday.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:39.080
There is a federal hearing scheduled to rule on a request for a preliminary injunction against

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.940
that new five year eligibility rule.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:46.920
If the judge grants that injunction, the NCAA's authority to regulate its own sport will take

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.680
another devastating hit.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:52.160
The broader question it all leaves us with is a bit unsettling.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:55.880
If the Supreme Court and the Federal Reserve are struggling this profoundly to figure out

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:00.080
how to handle a common weed killer and some computer chips, imagine what happens when

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:04.760
those exact same slow moving institutions have to figure out how to regulate human

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:09.160
gene editing or brain computer interfaces in just a few short years.
